Umm. Which part needs clarification?

Every spellbook has an (invisible) counter ('spestudied') that starts
at zero. This counter is incremented by one every time the spellbook
is successfully read or it is polymorphed. If you successfully read a
spellbook whose spestudied counter is greater than 3, you'll find that
you're instead reading a blank spellbook.

That's all there is to it; you can't reverse this degradation.

